    "created_at": "2022-02-24T09:59:02Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-02-24T09:59:02Z",
    "body": "I'm not sure if the spec changed, but it now does require `currentTime` to immediately start returning the new value. In https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-media-currenttime says:\r\n> On setting, if the [media element](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#media-element)'s [`readyState`](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-media-readystate) is [`HAVE_NOTHING`](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-media-have_nothing), then it must set the [media element](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#media-element)'s [default playback start position](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#default-playback-start-position) to the new value; otherwise, it must set the [official playback position](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#official-playback-position) to the new value and then [seek](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-media-seek) to the new value.\r\n\r\nThe official playback position is what `currentTime` returns.",
