    "created_at": "2022-06-10T20:20:33Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-06-10T20:20:33Z",
    "body": "The currentTime value says it should be assigned to **default playback start position** when readyState is HAVE_NOTHING.\r\n>On setting, if the [media element](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#media-element)'s [readyState](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-media-readystate) is [HAVE_NOTHING](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-media-have_nothing), then it must set the [media element](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#media-element)'s [default playback start position](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#default-playback-start-position) to the new value\r\n\r\nBut the seeking definition makes no mention of the assignment.\r\n[4.8.11.9](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/media.html#seeking) step 2\r\n>If the [media element](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/media.html#media-element)'s [readyState](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/media.html#dom-media-readystate) is [HAVE_NOTHING](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/media.html#dom-media-have_nothing), return.\r\n\r\nCan this be reopened to clarify those definitions?",
